        "original_id": "681ac579-c0e4-59d5-b22b-45fc47656c92",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Oscar Wilde, Ken Russell\n- Works: Salome's Last Dance, Salome\n- Topics: New Testament, framing narrative\n\nFacts:\n- Oscar Wilde was born on 16 October 1854 and died on 30 November 1900.\n- Oscar Wilde was a prolific Irish writer who wrote plays, fiction, essays, and poetry.\n- Oscar Wilde wrote the 1893 play \"Salome\".\n- The play \"Salome\" is based on a story from the New Testament.\n- Most of the action in \"Salome's Last Dance\" is a verbatim performance of Oscar Wilde's play \"Salome\".\n- Ken Russell wrote a framing narrative that is also part of \"Salome's Last Dance\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a9cd4fd1-0a3d-5594-9445-ea83675d48a0",
        "text": "Page: Salome's Last Dance. Sentence: Although most of the action is a verbatim performance of Oscar Wilde's 1893 play \"Salome\", which is itself based on a story from the New Testament, there is also a framing narrative written by Russell himself.\nPage: Oscar Wilde. Sentence: Oscar Fingal O'Flahertie Wills Wilde (16 October 185430 November 1900) was a prolific Irish writer who wrote plays, fiction, essays, and poetry.",
